      "notes": "Segmented ACVP plus bounded core Wycheproof, Wycheproof ECDH, complete split Wycheproof ECDSA, security, general, and CCTV/stress/fuzz/slow evidence. AES CCM/CFB/OFB issues remain; CFB8 has one confirmed segfault plus pytest-timeout failures. Non-AES ACVP is complete with ECDH, ML-DSA, EdDSA, hash, RSA-PSS/SHA3, and SLH-DSA failure clusters; ML-KEM, RSA keygen, HMAC, and ECDSA are clean or mostly clean. Core Wycheproof completed without crashes/timeouts; failures cluster in AES, HMAC, RSA-OAEP/PSS/signature, and ML-DSA signing/verification. Standalone Wycheproof ECDH completed without crashes/timeouts and is a broad failure cluster dominated by mechanism-parameter rejection. Wycheproof ECDSA split shards completed with 28,915/28,915 passed and no skips/crashes/timeouts across brainpool, secp160/secp192, secp224, secp256, and secp384/secp521. Security segment found FFI arithmetic/length crashes, NULL mechanism crash, weak RSA exponent keygen segfaults, key-attribute boundary failures, padding/timing oracle findings, and clean KWP/RSA error-path/null-pointer/nonce/handle-reuse/Tookan slices. General slice completed without crashes/timeouts; clean areas include interface/init/interop/object/X.509 import/RSA extended and wrapping, while failures cluster in mechanism sign/digest/attribute/multipart/wrap, hash ML-DSA, session state, access levels, AES/Salsa/ChaCha, and BLAKE2. CCTV/stress/fuzz/slow slice completed without crashes/timeouts; CCTV and X.509 limbo stress were clean, while five fuzz failures returned CKR_OPERATION_ACTIVE in repeated digest/HMAC single-part operations.",
